0"},{"type":"access","description":null,"id":"14108","location":{"latitude":"47.88346862792969","longitude":"-93.58883666992188"},"name":"Alt.Access","distance":"10.1","photoID":"0","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"waterfall","description":"This will be the (whitewater) highlight of the trip.\n\nDrainage area at this location is about 962 square miles (per USGS StreamStats Beta software).","id":"14107","location":{"latitude":"47.91999816894531","longitude":"-93.62200164794922"},"name":"Little American Falls","distance":"18.25","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"116725","location":{"latitude":"47.9208984375","longitude":"-93.6213989257812"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"18.3","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"378843","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"378837","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Luke Surma","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/378843","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/378843"}},{"id":"378842","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"378837","description":"the little american falls at 144 cfs","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Luke Surma","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/378842","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/378842"}}],"detail":{"id":"946","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"**Quick Facts:**\n\nLocation: NorthCentral Minnesota, approximately 13 miles NE from Bigfork, 136 miles NW from Duluth.\n\nShuttle Length: 12.7 miles. (See details in \"Directions\" Tab.)\n\nCharacter: Northwoods canoe tripping, mostly flatwater, light rapids and one falls.\n\nPut-in elevation is approximately 1280'.\n\nTake-out elevation is approximately 1240'.\n\nThus total elevation change is approximately 40'.\n\nInformation (lat, lng, elev, total drop, run length, shuttle length) adjusted and/or verified from best manual extrapolation of online data (via maps.google.com, distance measuring tool, and other resources). 2009.04.15\n\nThe resolution on Google Maps for this area is pretty good. Go to the 'Map' tab, click 'USGS Aerial' 'Satellite', double-click near the put-in, zoom in to the maximum resolution available (without losing image), and do a 'virtual walk' of this reach!\n\n**General Overview**\n\nThis reach includes class I rapids, a half-mile stretch of Class II (Muldoon Rapids), and **Little American Falls**, described in a MN DNR brochure as _\"a six foot ledge into a deep pool flanked by 60 foot bluffs.\"_ It lists conflicting ratings for the drop, once calling it Class III-IV, and later calling it Class IV-V. (I anticipate the former is more likely correct by current standards.)\n\nBoaters may use alternate access to shorten the trip (perhaps even just doing a 'park-and-huck at the take-out falls?).\n\nCliff Langley provides (2011-03-21):\n\n_Little American Falls is a very scenic drop you can hike to from a trail in the Little American Falls campground. The falls is a class III+, or class IV if really juicing. It is basically one move, line up and go off a 4 to 6 foot drop. It didn't seem worth the bother of hiking up and down a long (hundred yard plus) staircase for one drop that would take 2 seconds to run. Nice spot though, cool campsite only accessible by water craft on river left right by the falls._","averageGradient":"2","maxGradient":"8","length":"18.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"946","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":"0 - 200 cfs  Likely too low (likely under 130 cfs). Areas of rapids/gradient likely to be scrapey. *** 200 - 300 cfs  Likely low, possibly E.L.F. (Extreme Low Flow) boatable. Possibly 130-200 cfs. WE NEED YOUR INPUT to refine/redefine gauge ranges! Create a \"Trip Report\" stating flow and your impressions (low/moderate/high).","lowRunnableRangeComment":"Possibly low boatable range (perhaps 200-400 cfs). WE NEED YOUR INPUT to refine/redefine gauge ranges! Create a \"Trip Report\" stating flow and your impressions (low/moderate/high).","mediumRunnableRangeComment":"Possibly moderate boatable range (perhaps 400-800 cfs). WE NEED YOUR INPUT to refine/redefine gauge ranges! Create a \"Trip Report\" stating flow and your impressions (low/moderate/high).","highRunnableRangeComment":"Possibly high boatable? (Likely 800-1000 cfs.) WE NEED YOUR INPUT to refine/redefine gauge ranges! Create a \"Trip Report\" stating flow and your impressions (low/moderate/high).","aboveRecommendedRangeComment":"Likely unusually high. Boatable? WE NEED YOUR INPUT to refine/redefine gauge ranges! Create a \"Trip Report\" stating flow and your impressions (low/moderate/high).","lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"300","beginMediumRunnable":"600","beginHighRunnable":"1200","endHighRunnable":"1540"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"BIG FORK RIVER AT BIG FALLS, MN","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"05132000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"743","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"4.05","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"48.19634308","longitude":"-93.8080272"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/05132000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/05132000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":"Gauge (1480 sq.mi. drainage) is 50 miles downstream. Flow here may be ~2/3rds the gauge reading. (Correlations are not assured.)","status":{"status":"medium-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"743","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qu